 core: `Saturn forms a trine to Neptune, 120 degrees in the same elemental family. Structure and dissolution are drawing from the same source. The planet that builds foundation and the planet that dissolves boundaries recognize each other as kin. Saturn's consolidation and Neptune's transcendence operate in natural harmony. When Saturn establishes structure, it allows what lies beyond form; when Neptune dissolves boundaries, it serves practical spiritual expression. This aspect produces grounded mysticism: structure that serves transcendence, discipline that allows surrender.`,
 behavioral: `You experience Saturn's structural requirement and Neptune's dissolving clarity as compatible forces. When you build foundation, you're already including what transcends form. When you surrender boundaries, you're already giving that surrender practical structure. This produces spiritual discipline that doesn't rigidify, consolidation that includes the mystical naturally. The gift is capacity for sustained spiritual practice where form and transcendence support each other. The work is recognizing when situations need dissolution beyond comfortable structure. The trine can make spiritual work feel too grounded and prevent the necessary surrender genuine Neptune requires.`,
