 core_synastry: `Saturn sextile Pluto between these charts means one person's structural principle and the other person's transformative principle are operating in compatible modes. Consolidation and death-and-rebirth can cooperate without competing. Structure and transformation have productive breathing room from each other.`,
 behavioral_synastry: `When one person's Saturn builds structure, the other person's Pluto can contribute transformative framework without demanding total destruction. When one person's Pluto transforms, the other person's Saturn can give that transformation structural form. The sextile means consolidation and death-and-rebirth support each other productively, neither has to dominate or surrender. Use this for shared commitments that benefit from both structure and transformation applied at different moments rather than simultaneously.`,
 friendship_synastry: `One friend's Saturn and the other friend's Pluto are sextile, sixty degrees apart. Structure and transformation cooperate productively in this friendship. These friendships often involve good shared power where discipline and intensity both contribute without fighting. Saturn maintains foundation, Pluto transforms what's obsolete, and both voices are heard.`,
 romantic_synastry: `One partner's Saturn and the other's Pluto are sextile. Structure and transformation cooperate in this relationship. When you face change together, both foundation and depth can be present without one crushing the other. The sextile produces partnerships where discipline and power support each other productively. Use this for building together where both people's capacities contribute at appropriate moments.`,
 core_transit: `Saturn forms a sextile to Pluto, 60 degrees of productive cooperation. What requires foundation and what demands transformation are operating in compatible modes during this 3-4 week period. Your consolidation principle and your transformative principle have breathing room from each other. Saturn can build structure without Pluto immediately demanding destruction, and Pluto can transform without Saturn experiencing it as pure chaos. This is access to flexible power where discipline and intensity support each other productively.`,
 behavioral_transit: `Consolidating and transforming feel compatible during this window rather than opposed. What you're building and what you're destroying can support each other without one dominating. Use this for commitments that need both structure and transformation applied at appropriate moments, changes where discipline and intensity are both present but not fighting, rebuilding that happens in productive sequence rather than competing simultaneously. The sextile makes cooperation available but won't manufacture genuine capacity for transformation where attachment to what exists still dominates or create structure where no foundation can actually be built.`,
